<DocsExample TExample="InputTextBasicExample" Title="Binding a value" Description="Bind with @@bind-Value. BindOnInput updates the value on every keystroke instead of on change." />
<DocsExample TExample="InputTextAppearanceExample" Title="Appearance and density" Description="Appearance switches between Filled and Outlined. Density tightens the field height." />
<DocsExample TExample="InputTextTypesExample" Title="Input types" Description="InputType selects the native keyboard and behavior: Email, Password, Tel (with PhoneMask), Url and Search." />
<DocsExample TExample="InputTextAffixesExample" Title="Icons, prefix, suffix and counter" Description="LeadingIcon, PrefixText and SuffixText add context. A native maxlength attribute enables the character counter." />
<DocsExample TExample="InputTextStatesExample" Title="Read-only, disabled and error" Description="ReadOnly shows a value that cannot change, Disabled removes interaction, and ErrorText forces an error message." />
<DocsExample TExample="InputTextValidationExample" Title="Validation in a form" Description="Inside an NTForm with DataAnnotationsValidator, fields show data annotation messages and the form submits only when valid." />
